From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kernel32, user32, oleacc: the functions NVDA binds at start

NVDA (the screen reader) binds its Windows functions by name with ctypes when
it starts, and stopped at the first one Wine did not export: SG Store's NVDA
installed nothing, its installer ending at once (found walking the store
catalogue, 2026-10-20). Missing were:

- kernel32.GetConsoleSelectionInfo (in kernelbase): a console reports no
  selection, as Windows does when nothing is selected; no console is
  ERROR_INVALID_HANDLE.
- user32.RegisterPointerInputTarget / UnregisterPointerInputTarget: taking
  every pointer of a type is for programs with UIAccess; as on Windows for a
  program without it, ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED.
- user32.GhostWindowFromHungWindow: Wine draws no ghost windows, NULL.
- oleacc.AccSetRunningUtilityState, AccNotifyTouchInteraction: noted, S_OK.

With them NVDA installs (asking an administrator) and starts. Gate
test-nvdabindings (64- and 32-bit); mutant SG_MUTANT_NO_NVDA_BINDINGS (user32)
and SG_MUTANT_NO_SELECTION_INFO (kernelbase) fail it.
---
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/console.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/console.c
@@ -1372,6 +1372,37 @@
 }
 
 
+/******************************************************************************
+ *	GetConsoleSelectionInfo   (kernelbase.@)
+ *
+ * Stained Glass OS 5941: the console's mouse/keyboard selection. Wine's
+ * consoles have none an application can see, so a console reports no
+ * selection, as Windows does when nothing is selected. NVDA binds it at
+ * start (winBindings.kernel32) and stopped with "function not found".
+ */
+BOOL WINAPI GetConsoleSelectionInfo( CONSOLE_SELECTION_INFO *info )
+{
+    TRACE( "(%p)\n", info );
+
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_NO_SELECTION_INFO
+    SetLastError( ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED );
+    return FALSE;
+#endif
+    if (!RtlGetCurrentPeb()->ProcessParameters->ConsoleHandle)
+    {
+        SetLastError( ERROR_INVALID_HANDLE );
+        return FALSE;
+    }
+    if (!info)
+    {
+        SetLastError( ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER );
+        return FALSE;
+    }
+    memset( info, 0, sizeof(*info) );
+    return TRUE;
+}
+
+
